  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is a cicada, and its body is not large. If Moonlight Gu is a blue crystal shaped like a curved moon, this cicada is a delicate craftwork made from palm wood and tree leaves by a master craftsman.",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Gu has a brownish yellow head and abdomen. Its surface has the texture of a tree’s growth rings. On its back are two very wide and translucent wings, like two tree leaves overlapping. The wings have the structure of a typical net-vein leaf: a coarse stem in the center, and from that stem a network vein of leaf lines on both sides.",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Fang Yuan’s memories of it at full vitality, its body is like a precious floorboard giving out a warm and glossy varnish, and its two wings are verdant green, like two soft tree leaves that have just freshly sprouted. After the first rebirth a deathly chill comes from its body. There is no shine or gloss. It feels rough and dim like dead wood. Its wings are fully yellow, like the withering leaves of autumn, and the tips are slightly rolled up and a little incomplete, like the corner of fallen leaves.",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "As it recovers, its two wings become tender and new like fresh leaves, and its body has a royal wooden lustre, while overall it still gives off a withered feeling of death.",
        "chapters": [
          162
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When both wings have recovered, it glows with a yellow and green lustre.",
        "chapters": [
          177
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the river of time it is a tiny Gu worm that spreads its wings, with a yellow green light protecting its body.",
        "chapters": [
          196
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At a later use it bursts out in two lights, green and orange.",
        "chapters": [
          399
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "During a later refinement it melts into a green jade liquid. That green liquid then takes shape and turns back into Spring Autumn Cicada.",
        "chapters": [
          1480
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "During a later refinement the cicada is a huge half-completed product floating about five feet from the ground. Its surface is not smooth: hairy and rough, with a metallic texture. As impurities come out it becomes smaller, and its metallic surface grows smoother, sharper, and brighter. It then shines in a metallic light and gives off a cold feeling. It shrinks to the size of a palm. The frozen cicada seems a work of art, very exquisite, and Fang Yuan pinches it with his fingers. The surface cracks, and a rank seven Spring Autumn Cicada awakens and flies out.",
        "chapters": [
          1645
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "changing-appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The Gu’s use is reversing time: Fang Yuan is reborn five hundred years earlier, carrying those years of experience with him.",
        "chapters": [
          1
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a river of time, and the Spring Autumn Cicada is described as the boat that crosses it. Going against that river leaves the world the same river; changes after landing then spread outward from the owner.",
        "chapters": [
          187
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Gu can be used more than once. Early text already says it is not a single-use Gu,",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "and a later chapter shows a second use. Landing points are not fixed to one moment: that second use returns Fang Yuan to the crisis on Qing Mao Mountain, not to the Awakening Ceremony.",
        "chapters": [
          196
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_awakening_ceremony"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After rebirth the Gu is extremely weak. Its recovery puts growing pressure on a low-rank aperture, and that pressure is what forces later uses as much as any enemy does.",
        "chapters": [
          187
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "As Fang Yuan’s first vital Gu, it was long ago placed under a seal of its own inside his first aperture, and having recovered for the most part it presses hard on that aperture even while heavily sealed.",
        "chapters": [
          969
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_vital_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It is a rank six vital Gu, and it remains rank six even at its weakest.",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan states the flaw plainly himself: it is not an Immortal Gu with a guaranteed success rate, and he could fail.",
        "chapters": [
          625
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan’s first use ends that five-hundred-year life and lands him on Qing Mao Mountain.",
        "chapters": [
          1
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "During the conflict inside the Gu Yue clan, a Photo-audio Gu replay of the Awakening Ceremony puts Fang Yuan on the wall as an image the investigators watch. That scene is a recording, not a rebirth landing.",
        "chapters": [
          180
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_yue_clan",
          "gu_photo_audio_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The same stretch describes the river of time and the Spring Autumn Cicada as the boat that crosses it.",
        "chapters": [
          187
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Driven into a position he cannot win from, Fang Yuan uses the Gu a second time and lands mid-crisis on Qing Mao Mountain.",
        "chapters": [
          196
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Left no defence against a rank nine Immortal Gu House’s full power attack, Fang Yuan self-detonates to drive his one remaining trump card. The activation fails: Spring Autumn Cicada has only just carried his will into the river of time when it crumbles and explodes into countless tiny fragments, and Fang Yuan is dead.",
        "chapters": [
          969
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "the-fourth-use-fails",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_immortal_gu_house"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
