  "distribution": {
    "locations": [
      "loc_river_of_time"
    ],
    "factions": [
      "fac_heavenly_court"
    ],
    "origin": "unknown",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Spring Autumn Cicada was the first rank six Gu of Fang Yuan’s previous life and also his last; he spent thirty years of fermenting, with all means and resources, to make it. Not long after it was fresh from the oven, righteous warriors gathered to kill him.",
        "chapters": [
          19
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Chapter 1’s surrounding enemies accuse him of killing thousands of people because he wanted to cultivate it.",
        "chapters": [
          1
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Later memory fills in the method and scale. He used a large number of mortal Gu to refine the Immortal Gu Spring Autumn Cicada, a mortal-to-immortal jump he later calls a hundredfold harder than converting one Immortal Gu into another.",
        "chapters": [
          408
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "gu_spring_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "To refine it he killed across more than ten thousand miles of land, and he states that he slaughtered over ten million people for that refinement.",
        "chapters": [
          379
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He later restates that he suffered untold difficulties and slaughtered many lives to refine a rank six Spring Autumn Cicada.",
        "chapters": [
          568
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the five hundred years of that life he could not obtain a blood path Immortal Gu; he had become immortal on blood path and designed blood path mortal Gu and killer moves, but without a blood path Immortal Gu he refined Spring Autumn Cicada instead.",
        "chapters": [
          1058
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The land spirit Ba Gui identifies Spring Autumn Cicada as a time path Gu whose historical master was Demon Venerable Hong Lian, the Red Lotus Demon Venerable, and names its aura as that of a rank six Immortal Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          383
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ba_gui",
          "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The Gu later receives a chapter under its own name, where Fang Yuan uses it a third time and lands still inside the blessed land at a different moment than the second use.",
        "chapters": [
          399
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "While Fang Yuan is learning how to search wills, so that he can work the Red Lotus Demon Venerable inheritance clues out of Mo Yao’s will, the text states that the vital Gu of his first aperture, Spring Autumn Cicada, had been Red Lotus Demon Venerable’s vital Gu in the past.",
        "chapters": [
          820
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_mo_yao"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Feng Jin Huang becomes Duke Long’s second disciple and asks who the first was, her father Feng Jiu Ge answers that her senior brother is Red Lotus Demon Venerable, and her mother tells her the subject is a taboo never to be raised in Heavenly Court.",
        "chapters": [
          1442
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_feng_jin_huang",
          "char_feng_jiu_ge",
          "fac_heavenly_court"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later text states that Red Lotus Demon Venerable created the Immortal Gu personally, and that it was his vital Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1477
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Still later, Duke Long’s side states that Spring Autumn Cicada was refined by his disciple, Red Lotus Demon Venerable.",
        "chapters": [
          1918
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_duke_long"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The same stretch that names the creation also states a standing cost: the owner’s luck is weakened at all times while they hold it.",
        "chapters": [
          1477
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It consumes the water of the River of Time as food. Year Gu shares that same food.",
        "chapters": [
          1129
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_river_of_time",
          "gu_year_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It is later sealed rather than spent, which turns it from a last resort into an asset that has to be managed.",
        "chapters": [
          671
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Inheriting Red Lotus’ true inheritance later gives Fang Yuan the entire recipe set for the Gu from rank six to rank nine: eighty-six rank seven recipes, forty-three rank eight, and three rank nine.",
        "chapters": [
          1435
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan then works a parallel refinement on it,",
        "chapters": [
          1479
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "and eventually raises it to rank seven.",
        "chapters": [
          1645
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Sixth Hair claims heaven’s will is hidden inside Spring Autumn Cicada, saying Ying Wu Xie has verified it and calling this the best evidence that every one of Fang Yuan’s rebirths was affected by heaven’s will.",
        "chapters": [
          1076
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_sixth_hair",
          "char_ying_wu_xie"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Inside Earth Mother Altar, when Xue Er asks about the future, Fang Yuan answers with a reply he had prepared beforehand, saying that although he had Spring Autumn Cicada he has already lost it.",
        "chapters": [
          1145
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path-origin-and-later-history",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lady_earth_mother",
          "char_xue_er"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
